* each selected cell's `C̃` chain (`ch4`, `pearl_c4.chain`), by the kernel;
* each selected row of `A′·F_B` and of `B̃·F_A`, and the whole `G = F_Bᵀ·F_A` (`peel_factors_a`, `gram`): by the kernel
  on the two `k = 128` cases (`G` row by row, joined by `PeelFp4Proofs.mapM_ofFn_some`); on `prod-64-nvfp4`
  (`k = 1024`, about 20,000 firings, some 30 minutes of kernel time) by `#guard`, evaluation and not a proof;
* each `P_A,i = paRow? (eTilde E a_E) (A′·F_B)_i` and `P_B,j = pbRow? (eTilde E a_E) (B̃·F_A)_j G`, so `eTilde` is checked
  in both halves (`e_tilde`, `peel_factors_b`), by the kernel;
* each cell's four K16 steps, `uWord? C̃ P_A P_B` (`peel`), by the kernel.

Each cell's `peelFp4` entry is then assembled from its parts by `PeelFp4Proofs.peelFp4_of_parts`, not re-evaluated
